he victors  crown of roses though she was betrothed  to Robert Baratheon and Rhaegar himself  was married to Elia Martell we all know  what happened after if I'd been a bit  quicker with my Lance if I'd chosen a  faster horse perhaps I could have spared  the kingdom from the destruction that  came after all if I'd thought to warn  Brandon stark against his rashness he  came to King's Landing himself demanding  Rhaegar return his sister poor fool if  he'd only known the depth of Aerys  madness he wouldn't have dared provoke  him  Ares ordered Brandon imprisoned and I  could do nothing but obey when Brandon's  father Lord Rickard stark came to King's  Landing to beg for his son Aerys burned  him alive  but I could do nothing but watch I had  sworn a vow to a Mad King and was honor  abound to obey Him even at the cost of  my soul Ravens soon arrived with dark  news for the king the Vale was an open  revolt demanding lyanna stark's return  Robert Baratheon was smashing any army  that dared face him Eddard Stark  Brandon's younger brother was marching  the whole of the north down the neck and  had taken Catelyn Tully  Brandon's betrothed for his own thus  winning the support of the Riverlands  the king sent Ravens to Casterly Rock to  beg his former hand Tywin Lannister for  help and no Ravens return a plan was  devised Prince Rhaegar would personally  lead the royal forces now reinforced  with 10,000 Dornishmen north to face  Robert of the Kingsguard Lou and Mattel  and I would ride with the Prince before  we left the prince confided in me that  when he returned from this battle there  would be a great many changes in court  despite my vows to the king  I confess I was excited on the march to  face Roberts army we were sure we'd win  we had superior numbers and we had  Prince Rhaegar his presence lifted the  spirits of our men and he looked every  inch the king he was destined to become  but at the Trident the guards played a  cruel joke  Robert proved the Baratheon words as his  army smashed through our lines Lu and  Martel was killed I fell in combat badly  wounded and could do nothing but watch  as Roberts Warhammer ended Rhaegar  glorious reign before he began and the  kingdom that would never be washed away  down the Trident with his life blocked  when Robert spared me insisting his  personal mace to tend to my wounds out  of respect but respect for what my  Kingsguard shouldn't survive one came  let alone two and one who should have  been I swore an oath to House Targaryen  and I failed them all that's left of  their fire is a single ember halfway  across the world surrounded by darkness  the gods were good I would still be  young in the fullness of strength for  whatever the cost I will not let this  ember go out this time I will not fail
 

